# Routing Structure

## Main Router Configuration

The main routing is configured in [src/routes/index.tsx](mdc:src/routes/index.tsx) using React Router 7.

## Route Organization

Routes are organized by feature and imported from separate files:

- **Authentication Routes**: [src/routes/authentication.tsx](mdc:src/routes/authentication.tsx)
- **Master Data Routes**: [src/routes/master-data.tsx](mdc:src/routes/master-data.tsx)
- **Stock Opname Routes**: [src/routes/stock-opname.tsx](mdc:src/routes/stock-opname.tsx)
- **Purchasing Routes**: [src/routes/purchasing.tsx](mdc:src/routes/purchasing.tsx)
- **Activity Log Routes**: [src/routes/activity-log.tsx](mdc:src/routes/activity-log.tsx)

## Route Structure Pattern

Each feature route follows this pattern:

```typescript
const [Feature]Routes: RouteObject[] = [
  {
    path: "/[feature]",
    element: (
      <ProtectedLayout>
        <DashboardLayout />
      </ProtectedLayout>
    ),
    children: [
      {
        index: true,
        element: <Page[Feature] />,
      },
      {
        path: "[sub-feature]",
        element: <Page[SubFeature] />,
      },
    ],
  },
];
```

## Layout Components

- **ProtectedLayout**: Wraps authenticated routes
- **DashboardLayout**: Provides sidebar and top navigation
- **GuestLayout**: For authentication pages (login/register)

## Dynamic Routes

- **ID-based Routes**: Use `:id` parameter for detail views
- **Nested Routes**: Organize related functionality under parent routes
- **Route Guards**: Implement authentication checks in ProtectedLayout

## Navigation

- **Sidebar Navigation**: Configured in [src/components/layout/Sidebar.tsx](mdc:src/components/layout/Sidebar.tsx)
- **Breadcrumbs**: Use for deep navigation context
- **Back Navigation**: Implement back button functionality using `router(-1)`
- **Route Constants**: Define routes in [src/enum/routes.ts](mdc:src/enum/routes.ts)
  description:
  globs:
  alwaysApply: true

